.TH CHTTPCLI_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_declare_scoped \- declare a scoped chttpcli handle variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

chttpcli_declare_scoped(name)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares a chttpcli variable named name with automatic destruction via
GCC cleanup attribute.  ___chttpclient_destroy is called when name goes
out of scope regardless of how the scope is exited.

The variable is initialised to NULL.  Assigning NULL before scope exit
suppresses the cleanup call.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_construct_scoped (3),
.BR chttpcli_declare (3),
.BR ___chttpclient_destroy (3)
